From: phpv <https://github.com/supanadit/phpv>
Subject: [PATCH] define php_int32 on LP64 when SIZEOF_INT is not configured

PHP 4.3's basic_functions.h only defines php_int32/php_uint32 when
SIZEOF_INT == 4 or SIZEOF_LONG == 4. On macOS arm64, PHP 4.3's old
configure does not define either macro, so the header raises "Need type
which holds 32 bits" and every dependent typedef is missing. On LP64
platforms `int` is always 32 bits; use that directly.
---
 a/ext/standard/basic_functions.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/ext/standard/basic_functions.h
+++ b/ext/standard/basic_functions.h
@@ -1 +1 @@
-#if SIZEOF_INT == 4
+#if defined(__LP64__) || SIZEOF_INT == 4
-- 
2.47.1

